source: crates/leptoskit_cli/tests/snapshots.rs
expression: "normalize(&stdout(&output), &scratch.path)"
---
Formats Rust files and the markup inside their `view!` macros, with rustfmt and the project's `rustfmt.toml`

Usage: leptoskit format [OPTIONS] [PATHS]...

Arguments:
  [PATHS]...  Files or directories to format. Directories are walked respecting `.gitignore`. Defaults to the current directory

Options:
      --check                  Write nothing; print a diff of every file that would change and fail if any would
      --stdin                  Format source read from stdin and write it to stdout
      --stdin-filepath <PATH>  The path of the file read from stdin, used to find its configuration
      --exclude <GLOB>         Skip files matching this glob when walking directories, such as `'**/fixtures/**'`. Repeatable
      --stable                 Use stable rustfmt instead of nightly
      --toolchain <TOOLCHAIN>  The rustup toolchain whose rustfmt to use, instead of the configured `rustfmt_toolchain` (nightly by default)
      --no-cache               Format every file, ignoring the record of files already formatted
  -v, --verbose                Print each file, what happened to it, and where its time went
  -h, --help                   Print help
  -V, --version                Print version
